    'register-contract': visual('compare', 'A calling convention assigns preservation duties',
      'CALL saves the continuation. Routines must explicitly save any required general registers. The following choices are agreements you impose on routines.', [
        node('caller', 'Caller-saved register', 'Caller keeps needed old values', 'If a register is scratch under the convention, the caller must preserve any live value before a call. The callee may reuse it freely within its documented result contract.'),
        node('callee', 'Callee-saved register', 'Callee restores before return', 'A callee that wants to reuse a preserved register saves the incoming value and restores it on every exit. Nested calls must obey compatible contracts.', [], 'push bx\n; ... temporary BX use ...\npop bx'),
        node('result', 'Result register', 'Deliberately changed', 'A return-value register is expected to carry a new value. “Preserve all registers” conflicts with returning a changed result unless the interface identifies an exception.'),
      ], 'Document inputs, outputs, clobbers, stack cleanup, and machine mode before implementing either side of an interface.'),
    'arguments': visual('memory', 'Derive argument offsets from push order',
      'A caller pushes second argument 11, then first argument 4, then makes a 16-bit near call. The callee pushes BP and anchors BP=SP.', [
        node('saved', 'Saved BP', '[BP+0]', 'The prologue’s PUSH BP creates the lowest two bytes of this frame. BP now points here.'),
        node('return', 'Return IP', '[BP+2]', 'The call mechanism inserted this two-byte continuation after the caller pushed both arguments.'),
        node('first', 'First argument: 4', '[BP+4]', 'The first argument was pushed last by the caller, so it is closest to the continuation.', [fact('Width', '2 bytes')]),
        node('second', 'Second argument: 11', '[BP+6]', 'The second argument was pushed first and sits farther above the continuation. Saving another register below BP does not move this offset.', [fact('Width', '2 bytes')]),
      ], 'These offsets belong to this exact 16-bit convention. Re-derive them when return width or prologue layout changes.', 'push word 11     ; Second argument.\npush word 4      ; First argument.\ncall combine\nadd sp, 4        ; Caller releases its arguments.'),
